TASK 2: ADR REPORTING & DOCUMENTATION

1. CASE NARRATIVE

Case Narrative - A 32-year-old male was started on Tab. Amoxicillin 500 mg TID (oral) on 1st March 2026 for Acute Bacterial Sinusitis. Two days after initiation, on 3rd March 2026, he developed generalized itching and skin rashes over the chest. He had no known history of drug allergy. Amoxicillin was withdrawn on the same day and he was treated with antihistamines. Symptoms resolved and he recovered completely by 6th March 2026. Rechallenge was not performed.

